  "readme": "# Silt Meridian Hingevault — Opposed Bascule Freight Well\n\n**PORTRAIT-001 / Creator A / DIFFICULT #2 — 1024×2048 · Draft/HOLD · NATIVE-UNTESTED.**\n\nFaithful *recomposition*, not raster transformation, of [Silt Meridian Twin Raised Bascule Rail-Ferry Exchange #37](https://github.com/techrote/sandmapsreference/pull/37) at immutable donor HEAD `e2b53fb95ea93576afdc15c114e29b853c4b2c05` (source `cybersand-canvases/2048x1024/original-industrial-transit-wide-silt-meridian-bascule-ferry-261120/`, 2048×1024). New independent geometry, fixed seed 2111202657, target `cybersand-canvases/1024x2048/portrait-difficult-silt-meridian-hingevault-261121/`.\n\n## Intent / routes\nA drylocked entered ferry and separate cargo hoist at upper west feed two **opposed, unequal-altitude raised bascule leaves** framing a *tall* open freight throat. Rather than flattening the two hinged bridges across a horizontal cut, the portrait stacks the left hinge above the right and moves the ten-spoke rail indexer to a lower right-bank ledge; graded rail dispatch and entered customs fall further down. A distinct west lower winch/under-invert service return and central lower recovery preserve branch/rejoin options. True perpendicular orthographic side elevation, no platform tops.\n\nUpper site route: Ferry Bridge → Crane Sky Hook → West Leaf Reveal → East Leaf Reveal. Main route: Western Approach → Entered Freight Hold → Quay Manifest → Cargo Cage → Channel Throat → Entered Rotor → Freight Frog → Customs Examination. Service recovery: West Lower Winch → West Mid Service → West Under-Invert → Central Recovery → Dispatch Repair. Full concrete coordinates and obstruction scenario are in `receipt.json` and `plan.json`.\n\n## Rebuild & proof\nRun `node build.cjs` in this folder (standard Node 22, no dependencies). The deterministic builder reads committed `design.json` and regenerates complete Setup-v2, lossless disjoint rectangle replay, full indexed-material overview and six actual 1:1 PNG crops, route/grounding/material receipt, `exemplar.json` and `aspect_transfer.json`. No reference art or AI images are involved. `setup.json` is directly derived from 2,097,152 real cells, not a partial patch. Final nonzero IDs 58,62,100 are source-authorized inert solids; no initial fluids or powder. Checks use exact 19×15,23×19,31×27 in-bounds full Midge envelopes, literal endpoints, 4-neighbour BFS, a real obstruction and unshifted recovery. No native gameplay or persistence acceptance is asserted.\n\n**Acceptance gates:** independent Art/Technical/Shepherd same-HEAD review and actual Godot/Workbench/CyberDemoBridge/Rapier load, piloting and save-reopen are outstanding. No merge/Ready. Source and engine are read-only. Avoid treating diagrammatic raised bascules or static indexer as already-animated machines.\n\n**Obstructed cross-mooring route:** Western Approach → Mooring Customs Beacon, genuinely blocked by solid [170,320,104,64], must retain all destinations at conservative 31×27 and show longer distance.\n",
